Z||000000||Synth0id||08-08-2000||10:10 AM||||Hey guys,<P>I was reading some of the posts and i noticed that u guys talk about EGR. What is an EGR?<P>By the way im not too mechanically inclined(YET!) so if u could explain in "laymans" terms that would be great....<P>Thanx,<P>Synth0id||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||08-08-2000||10:34 AM||||The EGR is an Exhaust Gas Recirculator. Basically it take unburnt gasses in the exhaust and puts them back into the intake system. This helps cut down the NoX pollutants in the exhaust. When operating correctly it aids in regulating engine head temps and cuts down pinging. (predetonation)<BR>When they go bad they can cause problems. Especially when they cause vacuum leaks. Usually of Fiero's there is a pipe that goes from the EGR to the intake. When these crack or leak usually the idle goes up, Car runs bad and engine temps go up. Blocking off or removing the EGR will cause your NoX readings to increase which could affect your smog testing (if you have to have the car tested)But from a performance stand point if other things are adjusted (timing and fuel) you can get better efficentcy out of the engine. (runs better and better gas milage)I canoot say if there is any actual horsepower gain but accelleration is better.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Synth0id||08-08-2000||10:39 AM||||<BR>Thanx Oreif.....that was quite easy to understand. I appreciate it!<P>Synth0id||||reg||1
